{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 40, "timestamp": 1793253893, "idle_time_limit": 5.0, "env": {"SHELL": null, "TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "title": "kubeagt fix on 04-redis-combined (kind, rules only)"}
[0.004194, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m kubeagt fix -n redis-demo --context kind-kubeagt-test --llm none\r\n"]
[1.132944, "o", "LLM: off (disabled); using deterministic rules only.\r\n"]
[1.691627, "o", "kubeagt: namespace redis-demo, context kind-kubeagt-test\r\nFound 3 problem(s) and 3 related symptom(s):\r\n  [critical] Deployment/redis: nodeSelector redisnode=true matches no node\r\n  [warning] Deployment/redis container redis: memory limit 5Mi is far too small\r\n  [critical] Deployment/redis container redis: readinessProbe checks port 5432 but the container listens on 6379\r\n  [symptom] Deployment/redis: pod cannot be scheduled\r\n  [symptom] Service/redis: Service has no ready endpoints\r\n  [symptom] Deployment/redis: 0/1 replicas ready\r\n"]
[1.741641, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nProposed fix 1   source: deterministic rule nodeselector-no-match   confidence: high\r\nTarget:    Deployment/redis   namespace: redis-demo   context: kind-kubeagt-test\r\nProblem:   nodeSelector redisnode=true matches no node\r\n"]
[1.741861, "o", "Diagnosis: Pods of Deployment/redis can never be scheduled: the nodeSelector requires\r\n           redisnode=true, and no node carries that label.\r\nEvidence:\r\n  - Deployment/redis spec.template.spec.nodeSelector = {redisnode=true}\r\n  - 1 node(s) in the cluster, none has label(s) redisnode=true\r\n"]
[1.74194, "o", "  - node labels: kubeagt-test-control-plane: kubernetes.io/arch=amd64,\r\n      kubernetes.io/hostname=kubeagt-test-control-plane, kubernetes.io/os=linux, node-\r\n      role.kubernetes.io/control-plane=\r\n  - event FailedScheduling on Pod/redis-7758c4c5b9-7lmnk (x1): 0/1 nodes are available: 1 node(s)\r\n      didn't match Pod's node affinity/selector. no new claims to deallocate, preemption: 0/1 nodes\r\n      are available: 1 Preemption is not helpful for scheduling.\r\nChange:    remove the nodeSelector\r\n"]
[1.745276, "o", "    --- Deployment/redis (current)\r\n    +++ Deployment/redis (proposed)\r\n    @@ -39,6 +39,4 @@\r\n             terminationMessagePolicy: File\r\n           dnsPolicy: ClusterFirst\r\n    -      nodeSelector:\r\n    -        redisnode: 'true'\r\n           restartPolicy: Always\r\n           schedulerName: default-scheduler\r\nWhy:       Removing the selector lets the scheduler place the pod on any node. The alternative is to\r\n           label a node (kubectl label node <node> redisnode=true), which is right if the workload\r\n           truly needs special hardware; kubeagt does not modify nodes, so it proposes the workload-\r\n           side change.\r\nCommand:   kubectl patch deployment redis -n redis-demo --type json -p '[{\"op\": \"remove\", \"path\": \"/spec/template/spec/nodeSelector\"}]'\r\n==============================================================================\r\n"]
[1.745314, "o", "Apply this fix? [y]es / [n]o / [s]kip / [q]uit: "]
[6.29658, "o", "y"]
[6.647133, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.894808, "o", "  applied: deployment.apps/redis patched\r\n"]
[6.894992, "o", "  verifying: waiting up to 15s for rollout of Deployment/redis...\r\n"]
[22.706564, "o", "  verify: failed\r\n    rollout_check: fail: rollout did not complete\r\n    log_check: ok\r\n    rule_recheck: ok\r\n"]
[22.7546, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nProposed fix 2   source: deterministic rule memory-too-small   confidence: high\r\nTarget:    Deployment/redis   namespace: redis-demo   context: kind-kubeagt-test\r\nProblem:   memory limit 5Mi is far too small\r\n"]
[22.754767, "o", "Diagnosis: Container redis is capped at 5Mi of memory. It may start while idle, but under 32Mi there\r\n           is no headroom: real load (data, connections, buffers) will push it past the limit and\r\n           the kernel will OOM-kill it.\r\nEvidence:\r\n  - container redis (redis:7.2-alpine): requests.memory=5Mi, limits.memory=5Mi\r\n  - pod redis-79c848ccd5-jznlx is running now with restartCount=0\r\nChange:    set redis memory request 128Mi, limit 512Mi\r\n"]
[22.756769, "o", "    --- Deployment/redis (current)\r\n    +++ Deployment/redis (proposed)\r\n    @@ -33,7 +33,7 @@\r\n             resources:\r\n               limits:\r\n    -            memory: 5Mi\r\n    +            memory: 512Mi\r\n               requests:\r\n    -            memory: 5Mi\r\n    +            memory: 128Mi\r\n             terminationMessagePath: /dev/termination-log\r\n             terminationMessagePolicy: File\r\n"]
[22.756798, "o", "Why:       Setting requests.memory=128Mi and limits.memory=512Mi gives the process room to run with\r\n           headroom for load. Tune these from real usage (kubectl top pod) once it runs.\r\n"]
[22.756818, "o", "Command:   kubectl patch deployment redis -n redis-demo --type json -p '[{\"op\": \"add\", \"path\": \"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/resources/requests/memory\", \"value\": \"128Mi\"}, {\"op\": \"add\", \"path\": \"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/resources/limits/memory\", \"value\": \"512Mi\"}]'\r\n==============================================================================\r\n"]
[22.756872, "o", "Apply this fix? [y]es / [n]o / [s]kip / [q]uit: "]
[27.308334, "o", "y"]
[27.658285, "o", "\r\n"]
[27.971207, "o", "  applied: deployment.apps/redis patched\r\n"]
[27.97147, "o", "  verifying: waiting up to 15s for rollout of Deployment/redis...\r\n"]
[43.963571, "o", "  verify: failed\r\n    rollout_check: fail: rollout did not complete\r\n    log_check: ok\r\n    rule_recheck: ok\r\n"]
[44.045035, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nProposed fix 3   source: deterministic rule probe-port-mismatch   confidence: high\r\nTarget:    Deployment/redis   namespace: redis-demo   context: kind-kubeagt-test\r\nProblem:   readinessProbe checks port 5432 but the container listens on 6379\r\nDiagnosis: The readinessProbe of container redis probes a port nothing listens on (port 5432 is not\r\n           one of the container's declared ports [6379]). Readiness never passes, so the pod never\r\n           becomes Ready and Services send it no traffic.\r\nEvidence:\r\n  - container redis image redis:7.2-alpine: readinessProbe.tcpSocket.port = 5432\r\n  - declared containerPorts: [6379]\r\n  - event Unhealthy on Pod/redis-74d8dfd58c-2xfb7 (x6): Readiness probe failed: dial tcp\r\n      10.244.0.162:5432: connect: connection refused\r\n  - event Unhealthy on Pod/redis-79c848ccd5-jznlx (x13): Readiness probe failed: dial tcp\r\n      10.244.0.161:5432: connect: connection refused\r\nChange:    set redis readinessProbe port to 6379\r\n"]
[44.047501, "o", "    --- Deployment/redis (current)\r\n    +++ Deployment/redis (proposed)\r\n    @@ -29,5 +29,5 @@\r\n               successThreshold: 1\r\n               tcpSocket:\r\n    -            port: 5432\r\n    +            port: 6379\r\n               timeoutSeconds: 1\r\n             resources:\r\nWhy:       Pointing the probe at port 6379 makes it test the process that is actually serving. The\r\n           probe type and timings are left unchanged.\r\nCommand:   kubectl patch deployment redis -n redis-demo --type json -p '[{\"op\": \"replace\", \"path\": \"/spec/template/spec/containers/0/readinessProbe/tcpSocket/port\", \"value\": 6379}]'\r\n==============================================================================\r\nApply this fix? [y]es / [n]o / [s]kip / [q]uit: "]
[48.598744, "o", "y"]
[48.949146, "o", "\r\n"]
[49.304175, "o", "  applied: deployment.apps/redis patched\r\n"]
[49.304383, "o", "  verifying: waiting up to 120s for rollout of Deployment/redis...\r\n"]
[49.970088, "o", "  verifying: watching logs of Deployment/redis for 30s...\r\n"]
[80.994114, "o", "  verify: verified\r\n    rollout_check: ok\r\n    log_check: ok\r\n    rule_recheck: ok\r\n"]
[80.994358, "o", "\r\nWaiting up to 120s for the namespace to become healthy...\r\n"]
[81.843059, "o", "\r\nSummary\r\n  1. Deployment/redis: remove the nodeSelector  [yes, applied]  verify failed: rollout did not complete; blocked by other issue(s): memory-too-small, probe-port-mismatch\r\n     verify result: failed\r\n  2. Deployment/redis: set redis memory request 128Mi, limit 512Mi  [yes, applied]  verify failed: rollout did not complete; blocked by other issue(s): probe-port-mismatch\r\n     verify result: failed\r\n  3. Deployment/redis: set redis readinessProbe port to 6379  [yes, applied]  verified: rollout complete\r\n     verify result: verified\r\n  namespace healthy: yes\r\n"]
[81.843615, "o", "\r\nAudit log: /tmp/demo-session/audit.jsonl\r\n"]
